The '''Backwater Bayou''' is a {{Skl|Fishing}} [[Locations|Location]] and the first island that can be accessed from the [[Ship Navigator]]. It is unlocked by reaching {{Skill|Fishing|5}} and speaking to {{NPCSprite|Captain Baha}} in the {{Zone|Fishing Outpost}}.

{{ZoneText|Talk to &2Junker Joel &fabout &2Junk&f, and how to trade it for &6valuable items&f!|Add and remove &9Rod Parts &fat &2Roddy.|Fish &2Bayou Sea Creatures&f.|Learn about &dFishing Hotspots &ffrom &dHattie&f.}}

== Features ==
=== Chapters ===
The '''Backwater Bayou''' contains [[Chapters]], which consist of {{Yellow|38}} tasks for the player to complete. Completing all these tasks rewards the {{Item|Pearl of the Swamp}}, which grants a permanent {{Stat|treasure chance|+1}}. These chapters can be accessed by speaking to {{NPCSprite|Jonesy}}.
{{:Chapters/Backwater Bayou}}

=== Roddy ===
{{NPCSprite|Roddy}} can be found here, who can help apply [[Rod Parts]] to [[Fishing Rods]]. To unlock his [[Abiphones|Abiphone Contact]], one must give him a {{Item|Torn Cloth}}.

[[File:Fishing Hot Spot in Backwater Bayou.png|thumb|256px|An example of a hotspot in the Backwater Bayou.]]
=== Hotspots ===
[[Fishing Hotspots|Hotspots]] appear in water to grant buffs and new [[Sea Creatures]] when the player's bobber is within.

=== Junk Fishing ===
{{Main|Junker Joel}}
Junk can be caught while a {{Item|Junk Sinker}} is equipped on a [[Fishing Rods|Fishing Rod]]. It replaces all Treasure caught. The following items are classified as Junk:

* {{Item|Rusty Coin}}
* {{Item|Busted Belt Buckle}}
* {{Item|Old Leather Boot}}
* {{Item|Moby-Duck}}

=== Bayou Sea Creatures ===
The '''Backwater Bayou''' has exclusive [[Sea Creatures]], including the following:
* {{MobSprite|Alligator}}
* {{MobSprite|Banshee}}
* {{MobSprite|Bayou Sludge}}
* {{MobSprite|Dumpster Diver}}
* {{MobSprite|Titanoboa}}
* {{MobSprite|Trash Gobbler}}
{{:Sea Creatures/List/Bayou}}

